# ALS Signal source import template (pipe-delimited)
#
# Purpose: This file records the Source details shown for sources that are
# initially disabled in the app. It is deliberately suitable for a future
# import function. The first non-comment line is the header row; each later
# line is one source. Do not change the header names without updating the
# future importer.
#
# Adding a source: locate the publisher's official RSS or Atom feed URL. Open
# that URL in a browser or feed reader and confirm it returns RSS/Atom XML,
# rather than an ordinary HTML page. Read the publisher's linked Terms, RSS
# policy, copyright notice, and reuse/licensing information. Record the exact
# terms URL and any rights contact. If no RSS-specific permission is stated,
# use the conservative values shown below: headline, date, attribution, and
# outbound link only; permission and commercial use are not verified.
#
# File structure: comments may be placed before the schema and must start with
# '#'. The first non-comment line is the schema/header. Every subsequent
# non-comment line is data. Blank lines are ignored. Do not add a second header.
# Validate the complete file before importing it; an invalid row must not be
# partially imported.
#
# Field expectations:
# source_id: required stable identifier; letters, numbers, '-' and '_' only.
# name: required display name for the source.
# endpoint: required absolute HTTP or HTTPS RSS/Atom URL.
# category: exactly News, Research, or Community. This value determines the
# app's internal category; do not use All.
# feed_kind: one of direct, complete, alsFiltered, headlineOnly, yahoo, google.
# The app enforces this value at import and after restart. headlineOnly and
# google feeds are used only for relevance filtering and display headline,
# publication date, source attribution, and outbound link; their summaries
# are discarded before display. alsFiltered and yahoo feeds are relevance
# filtered. Use complete only when the publisher's terms support feed summaries.
# enabled_by_default: exactly true or false. Use false unless reviewed.
# publisher: publisher's display/legal name as shown in Source details.
# classification: e.g. Open or public data, Licensed source, Headline-only
# source, Intermediary, Permission under review, or User-provided feed.
# reviewed: date the terms were checked, preferably 'DD Month YYYY'.
# fields_displayed: concise description of the fields the app displays.
# permission: specific permission statement, or explain that it is unverified.
# commercial_use: commercial-use restriction or 'Not verified.'.
# attribution: required publisher attribution and original-link instruction.
# terms_url: absolute HTTP/HTTPS terms or RSS-policy URL; blank if unavailable.
# rights_or_corrections_contact: email or other rights contact; blank if none.
# notes: operational limitations, verification caveats, and storage/display notes.
#
# Values are pipe-delimited. If a value itself contains a pipe, replace it
# with \|; replace line breaks with a space. The reviewed date is the date the
# terms were checked, not a guarantee that the publisher's terms remain
# unchanged. The user remains responsible for review.
#
source_id|name|endpoint|category|feed_kind|enabled_by_default|publisher|classification|reviewed|fields_displayed|permission|commercial_use|attribution|terms_url|rights_or_corrections_contact|notes
rnz-world|RNZ · World News|https://www.rnz.co.nz/rss/world.xml|News|headlineOnly|false|Radio New Zealand · World|Official RNZ World RSS; personal-use metadata source|24 July 2026|Exact headline, publication date, source name and outbound article URL only|RNZ states that RSS feeds are for personal use only and must not be used to aggregate content on other websites. Health Signal uses this feed only in the user's personal, on-device reader, displaying headline, date, attribution and the original link.|Personal, non-commercial use only; redistribution or commercial use requires RNZ permission.|Attribute the named publisher and link to the original page.|https://www.rnz.co.nz/rss||Verified RSS endpoint. Disabled by default; personal on-device feed-reader use only. No summary, image or article body is stored or displayed.
